# Circles Registry — TEMPLATE
#
#   cp circles/registry.yaml.template circles/registry.yaml
#
# Circles are sacred spaces you create and steward — your offerings to others.
# Each circle is a separate git repository for others to reach through portals.
#
# The copy you create is GITIGNORED and stays on your machine. That is
# deliberate. A registry names real people, their handles, the topic that binds
# them to you, and the URLs of repositories that may be private. Published, it
# is a relationship graph — the fact that a circle exists can be more revealing
# than anything inside it.
#
# Use roles rather than names where a name is not load-bearing, and remember
# that a topic line is a claim about a real person too: "Intimate partnership
# practice with <name>" discloses more than the name alone.

# =============================================================================
# Your Circles
# =============================================================================

